title: 'M1.6 slice 2 r2 reading: theft path is not a $flow node; ceiling coalesces'
summary: 'The theft path #web-endpoint -> #socket -> #approval-broker meets the 3-component threshold, but it is a one-row relay with no state or steps of its own (revoke, write socket.auth.theft, raise one card). Documented in .purpose and theft-card.ts prose instead of a new $flow: a spec node moves Appendix A''s count (47) and is the founder''s call. Past 8 open theft cards a theft coalesces into the newest open card (its chain row stays); counted synchronously so concurrency cannot overshoot.'
